WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
[Music]

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[U. S. Public Health Service in cooperation
with The American Film Center presents]

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.100
[U. S. Public Health Service in cooperation
with The American Film Center presents]

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.900
[About Faces]

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.900
[Narrated by Lowell Thomas]

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.900
[This picture is made possible thru the generosity of Mr. Cator Woolford of Sterling, Georgia.]

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:34.900
[Produced for the United States Public Health
Service by Sound Masters, Inc.]

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:41.900
[Screen Play Oscar Saul, Direction Owen Murphy]

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:52.000
[Supervision of dental scenes Frank C. Cady, D. D. S., U. S. Public Health Service, J. G. Williams, D. D. S., Georgia Department of Public Health]

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.000
[Silence]

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.000
[Music]

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:55.960
[Music]

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.149
[Narrator:] Will everybody in the audience
please run the tip of his tongue over his

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:05.149
teeth? In the spirit of the story please.
That's right, thanks.

00:01:09.789 --> 00:01:10.930
That's the idea. Thank you.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:17.930
And what do you find? Anything wrong? Bridgework?
Missing teeth? That's what I thought. Well

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.700
that's what the story's about. About teeth.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:33.250
About Danny Smith's teeth in particular. And
here's Danny applying for an important job.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:37.950
What do his teeth have to do with it? Well,
are they helping him? Or spoiling his appearance

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:43.659
and his chances? And if they are helping him,
how did they get the way they are? Just look

00:01:43.659 --> 00:01:44.450
or what?

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:48.420
[ Animated figure with a camera over his shoulder
running along]

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:52.729
For the answer to that we'll have to go back
through the years to the time when he was

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:57.909
two months old. Not thinking about teeth here.
No teeth to think about.

00:01:57.909 --> 00:02:04.350
And there still isn't much doing on the dental
front six months later. When Danny ruled over,

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:11.350
in the order of their appearance, his mother,
his father, and his grandmother- leading the

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:25.350
family group. What's going on here? You two
have discovered something. Can it be that

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:26.230
this is Danny's first --

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:33.230
[Baby Crying and Music]

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:41.120
Yes, that's what it is. Danny's first tooth!
There it is. All alone in [inaudible] and

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:02.880
then comes company.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.980
[Music]

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:11.980
Well, Danny's getting along in years. Here
he is way past two. His mother has planned

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.129
her decision. Listen.

00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:14.170
[Mrs. Smith:] Doug.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.549
[Mr. Smith:] Yes dear?

00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:18.010
[Mrs. Smith:] Let's take Danny to the dentist.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:18.879
[Mr. Smith:] What's the matter, does he got
a toothache?

00:03:18.879 --> 00:03:24.930
[Mrs. Smith:] No, but one of the women took
me to a mother's club meeting the other day

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:29.870
where a dentist spoke. He said that all children
should be taken to the dentist as soon as

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.760
their baby teeth cut through the gums.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:35.659
[Mr. Smith:] Now what could be wrong with
Danny's teeth at his age? Nothing.

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:42.659
[Mrs. Smith:] Well, I still think he ought
to see a dentist. You have some time tomorrow.

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:45.900
Why don't you come along and see what Dr.
Jones has to say.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:50.870
[Mr. Smith:] I think it's a silly idea. Danny
has better teeth than I have; more of them

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:56.249
too. I say forget the whole thing.

00:03:56.249 --> 00:03:59.299
[Music]

00:03:59.299 --> 00:04:06.299
[Narrator:] So they went to the dentist.

00:04:14.939 --> 00:04:15.170
[Music]

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.989
[Dr. Jones:] How do you do, Mrs. Smith?

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:21.019
[Mrs. Smith:] Good afternoo,n Dr. Jones. My
husband and I would like you to examine Danny's

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:21.269
teeth.

00:04:21.229 --> 00:04:22.370
[Mr. Smith:] How do you do, Dr. Jones?

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.190
[Dr. Jones:] How do you do, Mr. Smith.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.620
[Mr. Smith:] My wife does insist on having
Danny's teeth examined, although I don't see

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.640
why that's necessary. I'm sure there's nothing
wrong with them.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:35.340
[Dr. Jones:] Maybe not, but we can't be absolutely
sure of that until we've given his teeth a

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:39.590
careful examination. It may even be necessary
to x-ray them.

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:40.580
[Mr. Smith:] X-ray?

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:45.409
[Dr. Jones:] That's right. They're doing a
great deal with x-ray these days. In fact,

00:04:45.409 --> 00:04:50.810
I just received a bulletin from the American
Dental Association showing some of their recent

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:54.140
findings. Perhaps you'd be interested in seeing
some of them.

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.310
[Mrs. Smith:] I'm sure we would.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:59.050
[Mr. Smith:] Yes of course.

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:06.050
[Dr. Jones:] It's really amazing the things
they're accomplishing these days. These cavities

00:05:06.479 --> 00:05:11.690
were so small that the eye might have missed
them, but they didn't escape the x-ray.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:15.090
[Mr. Smith:] Yes, but if they're so small
they can't be harmful [inaudible].

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:20.930
[Dr. Jones:] Well, if a cavity is neglected,
it always develops into a large one. Treatment

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:27.930
becomes more unpleasant. Takes more time and
costs more money. Now here. This tooth was

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:34.669
filled as soon as decay appeared. And this
tooth was neglected and the decay spread.

00:05:34.669 --> 00:05:39.199
If such a condition is not corrected, it will
result in the loss of the tooth.

00:05:39.199 --> 00:05:43.560
[Mrs. Smith:] But is that serious Dr. Jones?
After all, they are only baby teeth.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:49.520
[Dr. Jones:] Yes they're baby teeth, but they're
very important nevertheless. If they're decayed,

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:54.139
they will interfere with the child's ability
to chew his food and may have a bad effect

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:59.930
on his general health. But that's only part
of the story. Early loss of a baby tooth may

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:02.160
cause the adult teeth to come in crooked.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.020
[Mrs. Smith:] Well, it seems as if the baby
teeth are important after all.

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:08.370
[Mr. Smith:] As usual, my wife was right.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:13.419
[Dr. Jones:] There is still another important
reason for coming here [in?] time. The child's

00:06:13.419 --> 00:06:18.970
first experience with a dentist will be a
pleasant one. It means an examination. Possibly

00:06:18.970 --> 00:06:24.250
an x-ray. And a cleaning. Consequently he
won't mind coming for a periodic checkup.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.919
[Mrs. Smith:] I'd like to know if Danny's
teeth are all right.

00:06:27.919 --> 00:06:30.930
[Dr. Jones:] Then let's get started.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:31.430
[Music]

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:37.289
[Narrator:] And Dr. Jones makes friends with
Danny. Makes him feel right at home. Child

00:06:37.289 --> 00:06:43.030
psychology they call it nowadays.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:47.610
[Music]

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:54.610
Danny is at ease. He has complete confidence
in the doctor. The examination is all part

00:07:09.940 --> 00:07:16.940
of the fun. Danny enjoys it . And his parents
are relieved, for as Dr. Jones predicted,

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:20.030
Danny's first visit to the dentist has been
a pleasant one.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:24.690
It will be remembered as good fun. When the
time for the next visit rolls around, four

00:07:24.690 --> 00:07:29.610
months from now, Danny won't have to be coaxed
and the visit was an informative one for Danny's

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:33.449
parents. They learned a great many surprising
things about teeth that day.

00:07:33.449 --> 00:07:38.930
For instance, Dr. Jones told the Smiths they
could walk along anywhere and stop almost

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:43.389
anybody and find that they have decayed teeth.
Yes, anybody at all.

00:07:43.389 --> 00:07:50.389
This young woman for instance. She is unaware
of her neglect, but look. The x-ray reveals

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:55.479
a filling which represents previous decay
taken care of, but here is a new cavity that

00:07:55.479 --> 00:07:57.159
needs immediate attention.

00:07:57.159 --> 00:08:03.539
What of this enterprising young merchant selling
service with a smile? A happy lad with laughing,

00:08:03.539 --> 00:08:07.860
merry eyes. And currently he has rhythm and
maybe a song in his heart.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:13.669
Woe is the day his teeth have decay. Observe.
The x-ray shows he has a large cavity in a

00:08:13.669 --> 00:08:20.509
baby tooth that he will soon lose. And a new
cavity on the biting surface of a second tooth.

00:08:20.509 --> 00:08:26.500
Baby teeth growing out. Second teeth coming
in and decay in both. Yes sir, coming and

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:27.009
going.

00:08:27.009 --> 00:08:33.520
The doctor told the Smiths, such as this retired
lawmaker, wise enough to make a nation's laws,

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:36.669
but not wise enough to take care of his teeth.

00:08:36.669 --> 00:08:43.180
Just roll your eyes over this x-ray. Abscess.
Decay. Anything wrong? Is there anything that

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.680
isn't wrong?.

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:50.569
Let's examine the case of this in-a-hurry
gentleman. At one time or another almost everybody

00:08:50.569 --> 00:08:56.630
has decayed teeth and what do most of them
do? Well, let's see what he does.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:02.000
He thinks it over very carefully. Decides
he's too busy to take care of a little cavity.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.459
It doesn't hurt and after all, what's a little
cavity?

00:09:06.459 --> 00:09:11.810
Months go by. And a year goes by. And then
what happens? The little cavity has become

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:18.810
a big cavity. And the little pain is a big
pain. So suddenly he's not too busy.

00:09:24.609 --> 00:09:31.609
[Music]

00:09:31.899 --> 00:09:38.899
He wouldn't bother with a cavity, so he'll
have to bother with bridgework. And he didn't

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:49.890
want to run up a little bill, so now it's
a big bill. After all, what's a little cavity?

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:59.040
Getting back to the Smiths, Dr. Jones told
them there are three ways of brushing teeth.

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:06.040
This way, from side to side. Or the floor
washing method. Very effective for washing

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.290
floors.

00:10:07.290 --> 00:10:14.290
This is known as the circular or window washing
treatment. Also very effective for washing

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:17.250
windows.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:23.420
And here's the right way. The upper teeth
are brushed with a downward motion. The lower

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:28.600
teeth with an upward motion. And the chewing
surfaces are brushed by putting the brush

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:35.410
into the grooves and vibrating it backward
and forward. Sounds complicated, but anybody

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:36.550
can learn.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:43.550
Well, here's Danny again. Eight years old
today. And having himself a time celebrating

00:10:44.279 --> 00:10:51.149
the occasion. Danny's building himself up
to a terrific case of odontology. Toothache

00:10:51.149 --> 00:10:53.019
to you.

00:10:53.019 --> 00:10:58.850
And a toothache by any name hurts just as
much, as Danny is beginning to find out. Teeth

00:10:58.850 --> 00:11:00.940
can take so much punishment from sweets.

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:06.070
As we can see in this picture of decay getting
started [in the?] first tooth. Then slowly

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:11.070
cutting through until the tooth has become
infected at the end of the one of the roots.

00:11:11.070 --> 00:11:17.279
Yes, Danny doesn't feel so good. He has a
very low opinion of candy at the moment.

00:11:17.279 --> 00:11:22.310
It wasn't all the candy's fault, as Mrs. Smith
realizes. She hasn't followed through on Danny's

00:11:22.310 --> 00:11:28.089
teeth. She kept the appointments for several
years and then well, like a lot of mothers,

00:11:28.089 --> 00:11:29.440
she forgot.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:36.440
Result? Trouble. Well, better late than never.
But unfortunately it is too late.

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:44.350
Too late to save the infected molar. For Dr.
Jones had to extract it to prevent further

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:49.700
complications. He told Mrs. Smith how serious
an infected tooth can be.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:54.990
He showed her how decay begins, and when neglected,
penetrates the enamel and attacks the inner

00:11:54.990 --> 00:12:01.380
part of the teeth. How, if permitted, the
decay spreads and spreads, sometimes causing

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:02.829
an abcess.

00:12:02.829 --> 00:12:09.829
And an abcess like this means going, going
gone. And Mrs. Smith, properly sorry, resolved

00:12:12.339 --> 00:12:17.579
that no such neglect would occur again. All
that 16 years ago.

00:12:17.579 --> 00:12:24.579
What happened to Danny? Well, our frantic
cameraman brings us up to today. And here

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:28.820
is Danny, a healthy, confident looking young
man of 24.

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:35.820
Here is his mother. A bit older. A bit grayer,
and if possible, a bit prouder of Danny. This

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:41.450
is an eventful day in the Smith household.
And the gay smiles and cheery banter of mother

00:12:41.450 --> 00:12:46.690
and son are just make-believe to conceal the
anxiety each feels.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:51.449
For Danny has an appointment downtown for
a new job that's going to mean a lot to him.

00:12:51.449 --> 00:12:57.160
It's the job he was applying for when we first
met him back at the start of the story.

00:12:57.160 --> 00:13:01.920
We asked you if his personal appearance would
aid in his landing the job. And what part

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:06.100
his teeth played, and how necessary was it
to take good care of them.

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:11.329
The answers seem pretty obvious in the light
of what we've seen. Good looking teeth and

00:13:11.329 --> 00:13:16.430
good looking appearance go hand-in-hand. If
you have any doubts about how strong, healthy

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:18.380
teeth complement a lovely face [inaudible].

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:24.760
This picture is about faces. There is this
young lady. Lovely teeth help make the lady

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:31.760
lovely. Nice teeth always help. We don't appreciate
how essential they are until we make comparisons.

00:13:32.649 --> 00:13:37.930
And speaking of comparisons, let's make some.
These gentlemen answer the purpose very well.

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:44.930
Would you say there was competition for Robert
Taylor here? Or here? Or here?

00:13:47.750 --> 00:13:52.709
After all, what's a little cavity? And here
is the business appointment that started us

00:13:52.709 --> 00:13:58.540
thinking. We sought to prove that good, sound
teeth are a must if we would be healthy.

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:03.800
But they are a must if we value our personal
appearance. We feel Danny has proved the point

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:09.240
of our argument. But what about keeping our
teeth that way? How does Danny handle that

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.639
much? Let's see.

00:14:10.639 --> 00:14:16.899
Months at the job. Long hours. Hard work.
And lost in the immediate troubles before

00:14:16.899 --> 00:14:21.779
him, Danny is forgetting. Forgetting that
important date he has with the dentist on

00:14:21.779 --> 00:14:23.399
June 18th.

00:14:23.399 --> 00:14:30.399
June 18th, Danny. That's today for the dentist.
Remember? No, he doesn't remember. Well, we've

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:34.050
got some bad news for him.

00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:39.480
He doesn't know it yet, but one of his teeth
is beginning to decay. The strange part of

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.600
it is, Danny takes [care of?] his teeth.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:48.709
For example, he eats good, solid food; very
little sweets. But his teeth are decaying

00:14:48.709 --> 00:14:54.490
anyway. That's how teeth are. There's no way
of stopping the decay except by going to a

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:58.509
dentist; having it removed, and the tooth
filled.

00:14:58.509 --> 00:15:03.990
Danny brushes his teeth every day, and properly
too. But that doesn't stop decay. His teeth

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:08.970
and your teeth need more than a bath. They
need a dentist.

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:15.019
Well, as you guessed, Danny has entirely forgotten
his dental appointment. In his enthusiasm

00:15:15.019 --> 00:15:20.970
for the new job, he has fallen into the neglect
common to so many of us.

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:27.970
He just doesn't realize how he'll look if
he loses that tooth. It does make a difference,

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:31.480
doesn't it?

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:32.990
[Music]

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:39.990
Danny is going to be just another man who
wouldn't bother with a little cavity. That

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:45.880
is, unless something happens. Unless something
warns him of the danger. Wow.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:50.380
Well, Danny got his warning. The cold water
did the trick. And he's lucky it happened

00:15:50.380 --> 00:15:52.040
before the decay had gone too far.

00:15:52.040 --> 00:15:59.040
Remember the pause that made him remember
he forgot. And before you and I can say, see

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:04.430
your dentist regularly, Danny will be sitting
in the dentist's chair.

00:16:04.430 --> 00:16:09.970
And the tooth has been saved. It has a filling,
but it has [inaudible]. And Danny's had a

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:14.100
lesson. He's going to remember to visit the
dentist three times a year.

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:18.480
He's going to remember that regular [inaudible]
treat decay and help guard against the loss

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:23.480
of teeth. That's pretty much the story ladies
and gentlemen.

00:16:23.480 --> 00:16:24.420
[Music]

00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:31.420
It's the story of Danny Smith. It might have
been the story of you. Or you. Or you. Of

00:16:34.110 --> 00:16:38.859
the fellow next door. The girl down the block.

00:16:38.859 --> 00:16:41.079
[Music]

00:16:41.079 --> 00:16:46.319
It might well be the story of this young man
paying his first visit to the dentist. And

00:16:46.319 --> 00:16:49.720
happily bringing our story to the end.

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:53.000
[The End]

00:16:55.000 --> 00:17:01.000
